Subject: [PATCH] lighttpd: tolerate ENOSYS from prctl(PR_CAP_AMBIENT_CLEAR_ALL)

fil-c's musl pizfix libc does not implement the PR_CAP_AMBIENT prctl subcall
and returns ENOSYS; lighttpd only tolerated EINVAL and treated anything else
as fatal (exit 255 right after startup, config test -tt included). Accept
ENOSYS too (same "not supported" semantics as the existing EINVAL case).

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -1903,7 +1903,7 @@
 	 * (avoid leaking privileges to CGI or other subprocesses) */
 	if (prctl(PR_CAP_AMBIENT, PR_CAP_AMBIENT_CLEAR_ALL, 0L, 0L, 0L) < 0
            /* not supported before linux 4.3 / on some emulators (e.g. Cloud Run 1st gen) */
-           && errno != EINVAL) {
+           && errno != EINVAL && errno != ENOSYS) {
 		log_perror(srv->errh, __FILE__, __LINE__,
 		  "prctl(PR_CAP_AMBIENT, PR_CAP_AMBIENT_CLEAR_ALL)");
 		return -1;
